  "body": "Yes, [`RadioNodeList`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/infrastructure.html#radionodelist) and its corresponding `value` property was a great step forward and solves many a use cases.\r\n\r\nHowever, in the wild, radio buttons are often used with a null form association, even though this is technically nonconforming. This means that there is no `RadioNodeList` to get their selected value or the other radios in the group. Since libraries need to be able to handle this case, `RadioNodeList` becomes useless for them, except perhaps as a performance optimization.\r\n\r\nIt would be useful to have a `group` IDL attribute on the radio button that is a `RadioNodeList` instance and is available regardless of the radio button’s form association.",
